{"type":"text","timestamp":1788418275782,"sessionID":"ses_f99f89748ffewmTPERPjSRhC5T","part":{"id":"prt_06609388800185eyZp4sB3ecLN","messageID":"msg_066093301001axGUcA00cxUIfo","sessionID":"ses_f99f89748ffewmTPERPjSRhC5T","type":"text","text":"\n\nThe implementation is complete. Here's a summary of the changes:\n\n**Changes Made:**\n\n1. **Modified `/testbed/src/tox/config/loader/convert.py`**: Added support for parameterized generic types like `list[str]`, `dict[str, int]`, and `set[int]` by detecting `types.GenericAlias` instances in addition to typing module types.\n\n2. **Added tests to `/testbed/tests/config/test_sets.py`**: Added 4 test cases for `list[str]`, `list[int]`, `dict[str, int]`, and `set[str]` parameterized generics.\n\n3. **Added changelog entry**: Created `/testbed/docs/changelog/3270.feature.rst` to document the feature.\n\n**Key Changes to `convert.py`:**\n- Added import for `types.GenericAlias`\n- Modified the `to()` method to detect and handle `GenericAlias` types (used for Python 3.9+ style `list[str]` syntax) alongside the existing typing module types\n\nThe implementation now allows using parameterized generics from both:\n- `typing` module: `List[str]`, `Dict[str, int]`, `Set[int]`, etc.\n- Built-in types (Python 3.9+): `list[str]`, `dict[str, int]`, `set[int]`, etc.","time":{"start":1788418275464,"end":1788418275779}}}
